IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch39-40`

-- Tests for chapters 39 and 40.  Every expected value was written from the text before the file
-- was run.  The translation's "and" in 39.2 is read as "and" (fork F39a); the other readings are
-- tested only to show where they differ.

§ `Tests -- chapters 39 and 40`

§§ `Chapter 39 -- the judgment of peers and the law of the land`

-- Arguments are the person is a freeman, it is done by the lawful judgment of his peers, it is done by the law of the land.
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- The text says "and": the judgment of peers alone is not enough, nor is the law of the land alone.
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Not a freeman: the text does not speak.
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 39 -- we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `set forth against a freeman, or send against him, otherwise than by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` AT 3
-- expect: MUST NOT `set forth against a freeman, or send against him, otherwise than by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land`
#TRACE `ch 39 -- we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 39 -- we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `set forth against a freeman, or send against him, otherwise than by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` AT 3
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 39 -- we will not set forth against him, nor send against him, unless by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `set forth against a freeman, or send against him, otherwise than by the lawful judgment of his peers and by the law of the land` AT 3
-- Reading B (fork F39b), either suffices: it differs from the reading taken in exactly the two rows where one of the two is present.
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- reading B, either suffices: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- reading B, either suffices: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- reading B, either suffices: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- reading B, either suffices: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- reading B, either suffices: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- Reading C (fork F39c), no exception to the passive limb: a freeman is barred even with judgment and law.
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- reading C, no exception to the passive limb: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 39 -- reading C, no exception to the passive limb: a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 40 -- right and justice`

#ASSERT `ch 40 -- right or justice may be sold, refused or delayed` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 40 -- right or justice may be sold, refused or delayed` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 40 -- to no one will we sell, refuse or delay right or justice` `to sell` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `sell right or justice` AT 4
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 40 -- to no one will we sell, refuse or delay right or justice` `to refuse` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `refuse right or justice` AT 4
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 40 -- to no one will we sell, refuse or delay right or justice` `to delay` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `delay right or justice` AT 4
-- expect: MUST NOT `delay right or justice`
#TRACE `ch 40 -- to no one will we sell, refuse or delay right or justice` `to delay` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: MUST NOT `sell right or justice`
#TRACE `ch 40 -- to no one will we sell, refuse or delay right or justice` `to sell` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

-- assertions written: 15.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
